# {{context|archaic|lang=en}} [[exceedingly|Exceedingly]].
#*{{RQ:Flr Mntgn Essays}}, II.7:
#*: Those which write the life of ''Augustus Cæsar'', note this in his military discipline, that he was '''exceeding''' liberall and lavish in his gifts to such as were of any desert{{nb...}}.

====Usage notes====
* The adverbial usage was very common in the 17th and 18th centuries, but is now considered archaic.

===Noun===
